error[E0277]: `User` cannot implement a sealed Verum trait
  --> tests/ui/compile_fail/includes_manual_impl.rs:10:33
   |
10 | impl verum::Includes<Order> for User {}
   |                                 ^^^^ not sealed by Verum
   |
   = help: the trait `verum::sealed::derive_facing::SealedIncludes<Order>` is not implemented for `User`
   = note: Verum's sealed traits are implemented by Verum itself and by its derive macros. Writing the impl by hand grants something no declaration authorises, and nothing would report the difference.
note: required by a bound in `Includes`
  --> src/domain.rs
   |
   | pub trait Includes<D>: derive_facing::SealedIncludes<D> {}
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Includes`
   = note: `Includes` is a "sealed trait", because to implement it you also need to implement `verum::sealed::derive_facing::SealedIncludes`, which is not accessible; this is usually done to force you to use one of the provided types that already implement it
